fcitx5-twpotato: the Fcitx5 front end of TwPotato (地瓜輸入法), a bopomofo input method.
Source code: @HOMEPAGE@

This package holds twpotato.so, an addon that Fcitx5 loads, and its two configuration files. TwPotato's own code,
this addon included, is under the MIT license (the text is at the end of this file). The Rust crates linked into the
addon are listed in /usr/share/doc/twpotato/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md (package twpotato, which this package depends on).

Use of Fcitx5 (GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later)

  twpotato.so uses the Fcitx5 library (libFcitx5Core and the libraries it brings in). Fcitx5 is copyrighted by its
  authors (CSSlayer <wengxt@gmail.com> and the Fcitx5 contributors) and is covered by the GNU Lesser General Public
  License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version. A copy of that license is in LGPL-2.1.txt in this
  directory (on Debian and Ubuntu systems the same text is in /usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1).

  - The Fcitx5 library is NOT part of this package and is not distributed with TwPotato. The addon is linked
    dynamically to the shared library your operating system installs (the Fcitx5 packages this package depends on).
    You may replace that library with a modified version that keeps its interface; the addon then runs with it.
  - The addon was compiled with the header files of Fcitx5. Small inline functions, templates and macros of those
    headers are therefore contained in twpotato.so. No other part of Fcitx5 is contained in it, and no source code of
    Fcitx5 was copied into TwPotato.
  - The complete source code of the addon is public under the MIT license (the address above; ime/linux/fcitx5 and
    ime/crates/twime-shell). ime/linux/build.sh rebuilds and relinks it against the Fcitx5 installed on your system.
  - The source code of Fcitx5: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5 , or "apt source fcitx5" on Ubuntu.

Other system libraries the addon is linked to dynamically, none of them part of this package: the C++ and compiler
runtime (libstdc++, libgcc; GPL 3 or later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception) and the C library (glibc; LGPL 2.1
or later).

